<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Ka'b</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bani Ka'b, Chaab</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Ka'b are an Arab tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> who rose to power in the eighteenth century around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shadegan">Fallahiyeh</a>, now Shadegan. As Safavid authority collapsed they built a sheikhdom with a river fleet on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shatt-al-arab">Shatt al-Arab</a>, challenging Persian and Ottoman forces. Their Muhaysin branch founded the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorramshahr">Mohammerah</a>, later ruled by Sheikh Khaz'al until 1925.</p></div>
